# Operator Catalog — Decision Operator Library

> Operators = internal decision scaffolding, never shown directly to the user.
> User-facing reports are always natural language.
> Operators are used to: compress the LLM's internal decision path, feed the validator, and let scripts parse/execute.

## 1. Action Operators (Action Ops)

| ID | Meaning | Params |
|:---|------|------|
| {OP_HOLD} | Keep current state | — |
| {OP_ADD} | Add / increase | {id, target} |
| {OP_REDUCE} | Decrease | {id, reduce_to} |
| {OP_REMOVE} | Remove / clear | {id, reason_code} |
| {OP_DEFER} | Defer handling | {id, reason_code} |

### reason_code enum
| Code | Meaning |
|:--|------|
| {THRESHOLD} | Threshold triggered |
| {BLOCK} | Blocking condition |
| {FLAG} | Flag triggered |

## 2. Risk Operators (Risk Ops)

| ID | Meaning | Params |
|:---|------|------|
| {RISK_STOP} | Stop-loss / halt | {id, threshold} |
| {RISK_HALVE} | Halve | {id, reason_code} |
| {RISK_ESCALATE} | Escalate | {id, level} |

## 3. Signal Operators (Signal Ops)

| ID | Meaning | Params |
|:---|------|------|
| {SIG_WATCH} | Add to watch | {id, condition} |
| {SIG_ENTRY} | Entry / trigger | {id, entry_point} |
| {SIG_EXIT} | Exit / leave | {id} |

## 4. Two-Layer Output Architecture

```
Layer 1: Operator JSON (internal, not pushed to user)
  → ~120 tokens · for validator · for script parsing

Layer 2: Natural-language report (pushed to user)
  → full style + analysis details + tables + risk
```

**Rule**: Operator IDs never appear in user-visible output.
